James inquired about making specific labels bold in ggplot, particularly for a categorical axis. I confirmed that while making all labels bold is straightforward using `element_text()`, selectively bolding only certain labels requires a different approach. I suggested using the `ggtext` package with `element_markdown()`, allowing markdown formatting for axis labels. I provided a code example demonstrating how to format certain labels as bold using the `scale_x_discrete()` function and custom label handling. The provided solution uses a vector to define which labels to bold, ensuring clarity and flexibility in label formatting.
